+//
+// Mirroring an even-width 4bpp run is a byte reversal plus a nibble swap.
+// Source byte i holds x = 2i in the high nibble and x = 2i+1 in the low.
+// With an even run start and even W, mirroring flips the parity of every x:
+//   x = 2i    -> odd  -> LOW  nibble of run byte w/2-1-i
+//   x = 2i+1  -> even -> HIGH nibble of run byte w/2-1-i
+// Both land in the same destination byte, with their nibbles exchanged.
